[{"id":21554,"sender_id":13,"sender_full_name":"Tim_Porter","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f5067a77bfb4640f798f193b25d43eba?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/graded.20algebras/near/21554\">#1</a> I have been writing up for the Menagerie (later to be adapted for the Lab),  a version of Turaev’s crossed <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>-algebras.  These are G-graded algebra for a group <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> which are Frobenius and also have a ‘crossed’ G-action on them.  Two questions:</p>\n<p>(i) in the entry on <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/graded%20algebra\">graded algebra</a> in the nLab there is a requirement that <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> be Abelian, but Turaev’s notion does not require this. Is this important for the Lab entry?</p>\n<p>(ii) I think that a graded <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>-algebra should lead to an automorphism crossed module /  2-group, basically <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U(L)\\to {\\mathrm{Aut}}(L)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">U</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Aut</span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>. Has anyone seen anything that mentions this (other than my paper with Turaev, where we use it).  It should be a ‘well-known’ construction, but I have not yet found it anywhere.  It depends on giving a graded G-algebra as a single object (?) monoidal category endowed with a functor (having some properties) to the category <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{BG}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">BG</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>","timestamp":1298889279,"subject":"graded algebras","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":21556,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/graded.20algebras/near/21556\">#2</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is this important for the Lab entry?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I wouldn’t think it is generally. For some applications it will be. Both cases should be discussed.</p>","timestamp":1298891548,"subject":"graded algebras","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":21558,"sender_id":13,"sender_full_name":"Tim_Porter","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f5067a77bfb4640f798f193b25d43eba?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/graded.20algebras/near/21558\">#3</a> I have upgraded <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/graded%20algebra\">graded algebra</a> :-)</p>","timestamp":1298901405,"subject":"graded algebras","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]}]